WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauds)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.963
- Please welcome Morena Baccarin!

00:00:03.288 --> 00:00:07.925
(audience applauds)
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:09.204
I love you!

00:00:09.204 --> 00:00:11.953
- Hi, I'm so excited to meet you!

00:00:11.953 --> 00:00:14.270
- I love your make up!
- Thank you!

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.750
- Oh my gosh, you're so cool.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.583
- Thanks, man.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.770
- Oh my gosh.
- I have help.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.900
- I'm not this cool by myself.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.570
- Okay, well that kind
of brings me right back

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.460
to when

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.100
I saw you in, let's talk about

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.220
a few of your projects.
- Okay.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.387
- If you don't mind.
- Sure.

00:00:32.387 --> 00:00:34.080
- "Deadpool."
- Oh yeah, okay.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.530
- Okay, you're so hot and cool in that.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:37.363
- Thank you.

00:00:37.363 --> 00:00:39.700
- [Drew] Any fly on the wall
moments from "Deadpool?"

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.020
- I will say, the second film,

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.550
I shot all of my scenes underwater.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:48.970
And that never made it in the movie.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.720
I was...

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.760
When I tell you in a
panic, like, I was panicked

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.820
the entire time.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.820
And I don't scuba dive, I don't do well.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.680
And it was like, it was
as if like, you know,

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.420
like it was probably another
10 feet above the ceiling here.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.550
And when you're like, you know,

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:05.940
I think this was the
word for "I need air,"

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.482
and then this was the word
for "Get me out of here!"

00:01:08.482 --> 00:01:09.315
(audience laughs)

00:01:09.315 --> 00:01:11.230
I was always doing this,

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.360
and they'd like, "Okay,"

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.420
they'd have to like,
destrap me from the chair.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.530
- 'Cause I'm sure you're weighted down.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.769
- [Morena] You're weighted down.

00:01:17.769 --> 00:01:18.602
- So that you're not floating up.

00:01:18.602 --> 00:01:19.435
- It's terrifying.

00:01:19.435 --> 00:01:21.620
- Okay, "Homeland."

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.540
Oh my God.
(audience applauds)

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.480
First of all, kudos to you,

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.870
you've got Mandy Patinkin,
Claire Danes, Damien Lewis.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.620
Like, everyone doing their thing

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.840
and you come in there with your moxie

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.130
and just meet the moment.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:34.963
- Thank you.

00:01:34.963 --> 00:01:37.320
They shot the pilot with
somebody else, unfortunately,

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.260
and it didn't work out for
whatever reason, as the mom.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.960
And I got the role and came in already to,

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.650
you know, a pretty gelled cast,

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.950
and the kids, they were like,

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.760
kind of putting me through
the ringer a little bit,

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:52.593
the kids.

00:01:52.593 --> 00:01:53.997
They were like, "So,

00:01:53.997 --> 00:01:54.897
"what's your name?

00:01:56.037 --> 00:01:57.617
"Uh-huh, you think you
can just come in here

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.887
"and be our mom now?"
(audience laughs)

00:01:58.887 --> 00:02:00.890
"Okay, let's see."

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.340
By the end of that day, we were besties.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.390
- All right, give me a
fly on the wall moment

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.050
from the amazing show "Gotham."

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.620
- Oh, wow.
(Morena laughs)

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:11.409
(audience applauds)

00:02:11.409 --> 00:02:13.080
That show

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.930
has a real special place
in my heart, of course,

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.420
'cause it's where I met my husband.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.340
And you know, we shot
together for five years,

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.140
we became a real family.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.200
I had a baby.
(Morena laughs)

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.140
That's him.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.980
He wrote the last episode
that we ever shot,

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.910
and it was a scene where...

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.440
The very, very last thing
we shot after five years

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.370
was our marriage scene,

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.190
our characters getting married.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.540
And it was, I'm gonna start
crying thinking about it,

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.140
but he like, he wrote
this beautiful speech

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:41.973
that Harvey gave,

00:02:41.973 --> 00:02:43.740
that was very, you know,

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.750
sort of personal to us

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:50.690
and moments that really
resonated with our personal life.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.567
Yeah.
(Drew cries)

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:55.730
(audience applauds)
Thanks a lot.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.960
- That's so much even
better than fly on the wall.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.190
Okay, tell me about "Endgame."

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.860
- Yeah, I'm so thrilled with how

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.750
they've been supporting the show.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.320
I don't think you can be a human

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.390
in any city in the United States right now

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.320
without seeing an ad or a poster.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.550
- [Drew] You turn and it's "The Endgame,"

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:14.430
with like, your sexy...

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.709
- Yes, the two of us, just like...

00:03:16.709 --> 00:03:18.090
(audience applauds)

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.173
It's a joke in my family,
bow to the queen now.

00:03:22.093 --> 00:03:24.200
So I play Elena Federova,

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.330
who is an international arms dealer.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.830
Who has orchestrated getting
arrested, essentially.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.440
So she can set in motion

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.440
with the fabulous Carolina Herrera dress,

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.150
that I found myself.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.310
- [Drew] And it doesn't wrinkle,

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.440
which is really impressive.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.476
- [Morena] No, it doesn't!

00:03:39.476 --> 00:03:40.309
- [Drew] I didn't notice that!

00:03:40.309 --> 00:03:41.142
- It doesn't wrinkle!

00:03:41.142 --> 00:03:42.287
- I kept watching, I was like,

00:03:42.287 --> 00:03:43.337
"It's gonna wrinkle, it's gonna-

00:03:43.337 --> 00:03:44.227
"No, it's not wrinkling.

00:03:44.227 --> 00:03:45.060
"No, it's not wrinkling."

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.300
- I wore that dress for
three or four days straight.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.910
I only took it off at lunch.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:50.743
- [Drew] It's so beautiful.

00:03:50.743 --> 00:03:52.210
- [Morena] They only
pressed it once in the day.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.123
Anyway, to go on about
what the show is about,

00:03:54.123 --> 00:03:57.790
she gets captured and even though my means

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.210
of going about things
are potentially illegal

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.650
and a little questionable,

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.400
what I want is justice and truth.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.460
And revenge for what
happened to my family,

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.920
which was orchestrated
somehow by the US government,

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:08.753
which you'll come to find out.

00:04:08.753 --> 00:04:10.000
I'm probably giving out a lot of secrets

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:10.833
I shouldn't.

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:11.666
- No, this is so good!

00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:13.250
I'm sorry to say, it sounds sick,

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.090
but everybody loves revenge.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:15.923
- [Morena] Yes.
(audience laughs)

00:04:15.923 --> 00:04:17.160
- They do!
(audience applauds)

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:17.993
- Yes.

00:04:17.993 --> 00:04:18.826
It's healthy.

00:04:18.826 --> 00:04:20.459
It's a healthy dose.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:21.709
- It's so true.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.990
Well, I happened to be looking
at your Instagram page.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:27.823
I hope that's okay.
- Of course.

00:04:27.823 --> 00:04:29.283
- I'm cyber stalking you.

00:04:29.283 --> 00:04:30.590
- It's there for the looking.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:31.423
- Okay, good!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.160
Well, we wanted to just do

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.060
a little quick deep dive with you

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:39.880
and see if we could ask you
some rapid fire questions

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.018
that we got from your profile.

00:04:41.018 --> 00:04:41.930
- Okay.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:42.763
- All right.

00:04:42.763 --> 00:04:44.860
You call yourself a wine
maker, late night thinker.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.480
What's the best idea you've ever had

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.360
while drinking wine at night?

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.214
- Having a third kid.
(Drew gasps)

00:04:50.214 --> 00:04:51.540
(audience laughs)

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.373
- Okay, perfect.

00:04:52.373 --> 00:04:54.900
Parlay with three kids
under the age of 10,

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.093
what is the best parenting
advice you've ever gotten?

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.853
- Just try to be good enough.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.045
Don't try to be perfect.

00:05:05.045 --> 00:05:08.045
(audience applauds)

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.710
- Okay.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.530
As a Brazilian native,

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:16.110
what is your first stop
when you go back to visit?

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:18.100
- I go to these little kiosks that sell...

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.470
They're like, they're lined with fruits.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.890
And you just make up a juice combination

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.304
and a grilled cheese sandwich.

00:05:24.304 --> 00:05:25.175
- The grilled cheese!

00:05:25.175 --> 00:05:26.070
- The grilled cheese is the best.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:26.903
- [Drew] They're flat!

00:05:26.903 --> 00:05:27.736
- It's the best.

00:05:27.736 --> 00:05:29.890
- The best grilled cheese ever.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.450
Well, thank you so much.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:36.640
Morena, watch "The Endgame"
Monday nights on NBC.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.520
And as usual, we'll be cheering you on.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:40.353
- [Morena] Thank you.

00:05:40.353 --> 00:05:41.301
- And admiring everything you do.

00:05:41.301 --> 00:05:42.539
(audience applauds)
- [Morena] Thank you so much.

00:05:42.539 --> 00:05:43.451
- We'll be right back.

00:05:43.451 --> 00:05:46.034
(upbeat music)

